  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Poverty Reduction Through Safe Migration, Skills Development and Enhanced Job Placement in Cambodia, Lao People&apos;s Democratic Republic, Myanmar and Thailand (PROMISE Phase II)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Recognising the impact of the COVID-19 pandemic on migrant workers and their employers, as well as the essential role of migrant workers in building back better, the overall objective is that women and men migrant workers have enhanced employment and livelihoods, contributing to greater economic recovery and resilience. It will achieve this through three inter-related outcome areas, in which more responsive policies are developed and implemented, by working with Governments, regional bodies and the private sector; women and men migrant workers have improved employability, including through increased access to skills development and recognition, and jobs referrals; and women and men migrant workers are able to take advantage of these opportunities as a result of receiving information and increased networking and protection.</narrative>
  </description>
